		### V3 ADDITION 4 - THE PARTNER'S ALLIANCE AND TRUCE ROWS ARE DELETED.
		### An alliance and a non-aggression pact are ONE pact between two rulers, so
		### the deal now carries them once, as the two mutual rows in the centre
		### column bound to tnt_alliance_p / tnt_truce_p. tnt_alliance_r and
		### tnt_truce_r have no writer and no reader left, so these two rows could
		### only ever have been invisible - and while they were writable they were the
		### double count the user saw subtracting points.
		### The surviving _p rows above are the pact, and they stay on the "what you
		### give" side because that is where tnt_val_alliance_p_value /
		### tnt_val_truce_p_value price it, and the sheet must never disagree with the
		### breakdown tooltip (user item 1.2). If a mutual GROUP header is ever wanted
		### in the sheet, block "tnt_sheet_multi_p" is the declared home for it.
		### THERE IS NO MARRIAGE ROW ON THIS SIDE, AND THAT IS THE POINT OF V4
		### REQUEST 4. There used to be tnt_sheet_marriage_r here, the mirror of the
		### deleted head row: same icon, same "Marriage pact" name, the same count in
		### its detail, and tnt_val_marriage_r_value in its points. Two rows for one
		### agreed couple is precisely what the user described as "you give one
		### character in marriage / the partner gives one character in marriage", and
		### it is not how the thing works: a pact is ONE object, and both halves of
		### its price are already inside that couple's own tnt_wed_net, one row in the
		### "You give" list.
		###
		### tnt_val_marriage_r_value IS NOT DEAD - it is still half the balance and
		### still appears in the breakdown tooltip. Only its SHEET row is gone.
		###
		### (tnt_spouse_r was already not read here: the script author demoted it to a
		### staging cursor, so it empties the moment a pair is committed.)

		### ITEM 2.2 - the partner's three multi-object terms, same shape and same
		### reasoning as the player's side above.
		### V6: head-row X inside the types here too, wired to the gate-free
		### tnt_sel_<item>_r_clear - same shape as the player's trio above.
		tnt_sheet_sel_title_r = {
			name = "tnt_sheet_group_title_r"
		}

